; Every word directive that general_directive() dispatches, except
; import and python, which need Python support (dir-import_py and
; dir-python_py pin them), and include, which the include tests pin.
; Each line of directive-word-table.dat takes effect where the reports
; below show it: a directive dispatched to the wrong handler, or not at
; all, changes them or fails the parse.  The journal lives in the .dat
; file because the semantic oracle does not read every one of these
; directives.

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/directive-word-table.dat reg
23-Jan-02 Grocery Store         Expenses:Food                $10.00       $10.00
                                Assets:Cash                 $-10.00            0
23-Jan-03 Bakery                Business:Expenses:Food        $4.00        $4.00
                                Assets:Cash                  $-4.00            0
end test

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/directive-word-table.dat accounts
Assets:Cash
Business:Expenses:Food
Expenses:Food
end test

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/directive-word-table.dat tags
Receipt
end test

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/directive-word-table.dat bal --flat --no-total --format "%(account)|%(tax_rate)|%(double(2))\n"
Assets:Cash|0.5|4
Business:Expenses:Food|0.5|4
Expenses:Food|0.5|4
end test
